# company: Arabic translations of the company strings (dojo/company templates and Python code).
# Searched before upstream's dojo/locale catalogs (LOCALE_PATHS in dojo/settings/local_settings.py).
# Only this .po file is committed, like upstream's catalogs; Dockerfile.company compiles it to django.mo.
#
# REVIEW NEEDED: first draft, not yet reviewed by a native speaker. Have a native Arabic speaker
# review every entry before a release that advertises Arabic. Entries whose English text is also an
# upstream string (Product, Active, Engagement, ...) override upstream's translation everywhere, so they
# keep upstream's Arabic (dojo/locale/ar/LC_MESSAGES/django.po).
#
# Update after adding or changing company strings (docker/company/README.md, "Arabic"):
#   cd dojo/company && django-admin makemessages -l ar --add-location=file --no-obsolete -e html,py
# then translate the new or fuzzy entries and compile.
